ServiceNow ITSM Foundations — Incident Creation & Escalation Review

Summary: Documented and escalated a service-impacting incident using ServiceNow's Major Incident Management workflow, from initial report through investigation notes and queue review.

Overview:

This project simulates the early lifecycle of a major incident: a reported service outage comes in, is logged per the Incident Communication Plan, investigated, and tracked through the active incident queue. The scenario used was a client-reported website outage returning HTTP 404 errors.

Environment & Tools:

Platform: ServiceNow Personal Developer Instance (PDI)
Module: Incident Management / Major Incident Management (Incident Communication Plans)
Other tools: none — browser only


What I Did:

Logged a client report: the website was unresponsive, returning HTTP 404 errors
Created an Incident Communication Plan (ICP0001002) with a short description of "Website is unresponsive," routed to the Major Incident Management assignment group
Investigated and confirmed the issue by reproducing it across multiple browsers — verified the 404 error appeared consistently in Chrome, Firefox, and Internet Explorer
Logged the investigation as a work note/activity entry on the record, timestamped, so the troubleshooting steps are auditable
Reviewed the active incident queue by filtering Incident Communication Plans to State = Open, confirming the record was correctly tracked with the right severity (Low) and assignment (System Administrator)


